  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe downward bias when recent history shows a sharp decline (e.g., Example 2, 3, 4, 5) despite low or neutral sentiment; forecasts fail to capture the subsequent volatility spike.",
    "When true outcomes show a massive upward reversal after a period of low prices and flat sentiment, the model underestimates the magnitude by failing to react to the 'mean reversion' signal in price history.",
    "Model forecasts are overly smooth and linear, ignoring the high-frequency volatility seen in true outcomes; corrections require adding a volatility multiplier during periods of low sentiment but rising price momentum.",
    "In scenarios where sentiment remains near zero while prices drop significantly, the model's persistence assumption leads to an overshoot in the downward direction, missing the eventual sharp recovery.",
    "Apply a correction factor that increases forecast variance when the last 5 days show a trend reversal against the model's directional bias."
  ]
}
